+    \since 6.13
+
+    Destroys the local data of the calling thread, if any. Afterwards,
+    hasLocalData() returns \c false for the calling thread. The local data
+    of other threads is not affected.
+
+    If T is a pointer type, the object pointed to is deleted. This is
+    equivalent to calling \c{setLocalData(nullptr)}.
+
+    If T is a value type, the stored object is destroyed. A subsequent
+    call to localData() creates a new, default-constructed instance of T.
+
